# Trivy's exceptions (ADR 0043): one vulnerability id per line, with a comment saying why it's
# accepted and when to look again.

# gosu's Go standard library (crypto/tls certificate checks). Every current postgres and pgvector image ships
# gosu 1.19, built with Go 1.24.6; gosu only drops to the postgres user as the container starts and never
# makes a TLS connection, so the flaw can't be reached. Look again when the postgres images move past
# gosu 1.19 (checked 2026-11-05: postgres:16-alpine, postgres:16-bookworm, pgvector 0.8.7-pg16-bookworm).
CVE-2025-68121

# openssh-client in restic/restic:0.19.1, the newest restic image. backup-tools only copies the restic
# binary out of that image and stops; ssh never runs, and the backup container doesn't have it. Look again
# when restic publishes a newer image (checked 2026-11-10: 0.19.1, pushed 2026-07-05, is still the newest).
CVE-2026-60002
CVE-2026-123158
